      "role": "user",
      "content": "the problem is that \"measured\" sounds too soft. if i'm too subtle, the labels and the industry will just brush it off like i'm some bitter nobody. they've spent years making sure my name never even came up in the same breath as the genre i helped build. i don't just want to talk about \"integrity,\" i want to expose the truth. i want to show people that the \"innovators\" they love today are basically just using my blueprints. \n\ncan we try something more aggressive? like a manifesto that calls out the systematic way they suppress independent creators to protect their big-budget investments? i want it to feel like a reckoning.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
